      "message": "fix(post): the lathe posts state G97 before a section that is not constant surface speed\n\nA section that posted G96 now cancels it at its end: a bare G97 right\nafter the main spindle stop (M05 / M5), before any after-operation word.\nEvery following section - a C-axis live-tool section, a drill on centre,\na thread, a tap, a probe, a speed-0 section - opens under constant rpm\nunless it states G96 itself, and no program ends in CSS mode. Before,\na live-tool section after a CSS turning section on the Fanuc lathe post\nstarted its live spindle (M1003 S3000) with G96 still modal, so its S\ncould be read as a surface speed.\n\nBoth lathe posts (fanuc-lathe.cps, tormach-lathe.cps) take the rule; no\nother shipped post writes G96. The clamp logic, the per-rev feed words\nand every program with no G96 section are unchanged; the only golden\nthat changes is nc/fanuc-lathe/facing_css.nc (one G97 after its M05).\n\nPinned by lathe_post_refusals (live-tool, thread and drill twins, two\nCSS sections in a row), lathe_post_tormach (the drill twin, two CSS\nsections), and the new recorded case css_then_live in every per-post\nscript suite (fanuc-lathe posts it; every other post refuses the C\nsection by name), on a test-bench mill-turn fixture with placeholder\nlive-tool words.\n\nFixes #1173\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
